<article class="env-lemma" id="02QG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02QG">Lemma <span data-tag="02QG">42.3.2</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $x \in R$. If $M$ is a finite Cohen-Macaulay module over $R$ with $\dim (\text{Supp}(M)) = 1$ and $\dim (\text{Supp}(M/xM)) = 0$, then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{length}_ R(M/xM) = \sum \nolimits _ i \text{length}_ R(R/(x, \mathfrak q_ i)) \text{length}_{R_{\mathfrak q_ i}}(M_{\mathfrak q_ i}).  \]
</div>
  <p> where $\mathfrak q_1, \ldots , \mathfrak q_ t$ are the minimal primes of the support of $M$. If $I \subset R$ is an ideal such that $x$ is a nonzerodivisor on $R/I$ and $\dim (R/I) = 1$, then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{length}_ R(R/(x, I)) = \sum \nolimits _ i \text{length}_ R(R/(x, \mathfrak q_ i)) \text{length}_{R_{\mathfrak q_ i}}((R/I)_{\mathfrak q_ i})  \]
</div>
  <p> where $\mathfrak q_1, \ldots , \mathfrak q_ n$ are the minimal primes over $I$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      These are special cases of Lemma <a href="/tag/02QF" data-tag="02QF">42.3.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>